twpotato: the engine and the model assets of TwPotato (地瓜輸入法), a bopomofo input method.
Source code: @HOMEPAGE@

This package holds the engine program (/usr/lib/twpotato/twime-engined) and the model and dictionary files
(/usr/share/twpotato/assets). It contains no input method framework and links to none.

TwPotato's own code is under the MIT license (the text is at the end of this file).

Third-party parts in this package, and where their notices are (all in this directory):

  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md    the dictionary and emoji data in the assets, and the Rust crates linked into the
                            programs of TwPotato. The file is the one of the whole project: it also lists crates and
                            components that only the Windows version has. The crates in the Linux programs
                            (twime-engined, and the front-end library inside fcitx5-twpotato and ibus-twpotato) are a
                            subset of that list; package.sh checks this when the packages are built.
  LICENSE-McBopomofo.txt    the McBopomofo dictionary (MIT)
  COPYING-libtabe.txt       the libtabe phrase list the dictionary derives from
  LICENSE-UNICODE-3.0.txt   the Unicode data the emoji table derives from

The engine is linked dynamically to the C library and the compiler runtime of the operating system (glibc, libgcc);
they are not part of this package.

